AIM:
To implement MST using Kruskal algorithm.

ALGORITHM:
Read cost matrix
Sort edges in ascending order
Select minimum edge
Check cycle using union-find
If no cycle include edge
Repeat until n-1 edges
Print minimum cost
PROGRAM:
#include<stdio.h>
int parent[10];
int find(int i)
{
    while(parent[i])
        i=parent[i];
    return i;
}
int uni(int i,int j)
{
    if(i!=j)
    {
        parent[j]=i;
        return 1;
    }
    return 0;
}
int main()
{
    int i,j,n,a,b,u,v,ne=1;
    int min,mincost=0;
    int cost[10][10];
    printf("Enter number of vertices: ");
    scanf("%d",&n);
    printf("Enter cost matrix:\n");
    for(i=1;i<=n;i++)
        for(j=1;j<=n;j++)
            scanf("%d",&cost[i][j]);
    while(ne<n)
    {
        min=999;
        for(i=1;i<=n;i++)
        {
            for(j=1;j<=n;j++)
            {
                if(cost[i][j]<min)
                {
                    min=cost[i][j];
                    a=u=i;
                    b=v=j;
                }
            }
        }
        u=find(u);
        v=find(v);
        if(uni(u,v))
        {
            printf("\nEdge %d:(%d,%d) cost=%d",ne++,a,b,min);
            mincost+=min;
        }
        cost[a][b]=cost[b][a]=999;
    }
    printf("\nMinimum cost=%d",mincost);
}

OUTPUT:
Edge 1: (1,2) cost = 10
Edge 2: (2,3) cost = 15
Edge 3: (1,4) cost = 20
Minimum cost = 45

RESULT:
Thus minimum spanning tree is constructed using Kruskal algorithm.
